voice-reading = Read these sentences aloud, at your own pace… { $secs } s
voice-sentence-1 = The baker on the corner opens his shop at six o'clock sharp every morning.
voice-sentence-2 = My neighbour painted his front door light blue during the summer holidays.
voice-sentence-3 = The tomatoes in the garden need water before the sun gets too strong.
voice-sentence-4 = The six twelve train arrived a little late this evening.
voice-sentence-5 = We chose a table by the window to watch the boats go by.
voice-sentence-6 = My grandmother bakes an apple pie and keeps the recipe a secret.
voice-sentence-7 = The cat fell asleep on the warm edge of the fireplace, curled up in a ball.
voice-sentence-8 = Remember to switch off the garage light before locking the house.
voice-sentence-9 = Monday's meeting has moved to Wednesday, just after lunch.
voice-sentence-10 = A cool wind blows along the beach and the kites dance in the sky.
voice-sentence-11 = The postman left a rather heavy parcel in front of the workshop door.
voice-sentence-12 = Every Sunday the market square fills with fruit, flowers and cheese.
voice-sentence-13 = I found an old radio in the attic that still works perfectly well.
voice-sentence-14 = This year the city museum shows old maps and brass compasses.
voice-sentence-15 = The children built a wooden hut at the far end of their uncle's garden.
voice-sentence-16 = This mountain path climbs gently up to a lake with very still water.
voice-sentence-17 = The cook tastes the soup, adds a pinch of salt and a little pepper.
voice-sentence-18 = Our team finished the project two days earlier than planned.
voice-sentence-19 = The library also lends board games and vinyl records.
voice-sentence-20 = The pilot expects to land on time with a temperature of twenty degrees.
voice-sentence-21 = A light mist covers the valley when we leave the village at dawn.
voice-sentence-22 = My brother collects stamps from countries I have never heard of.
voice-sentence-23 = The gardener gently prunes the roses so they bloom again in spring.
voice-sentence-24 = Before leaving, check the windows, the front door and the kitchen gas.
